  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The spiral round eliminates the join-bump that marks the start of each round in standard joined construction by never stopping to slip stitch. The hook works continuously; a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stitch-marker"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "stitch marker"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " moved up at the start of each revolution keeps count. The finished disc looks identical to a joined-round circle from the top but has no visible jog at the round start, which matters for colourwork and for motifs where the join would fall in an obvious position."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 20 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, stitch marker (required)."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 10 cm diameter. The stitch count and increase pattern are identical to the flat circle motif; only the construction method differs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
